# HPR: playback at speed through the Elliptic-BLEP resampler. A drum loop (the
# bursts) and a pad (a looped sine) glide from 1x to 3x over six beats, each
# running through `resample=iir` (the default); a second pad does the same
# through `cubic`, hard-panned right, to show both methods pass the same
# checks. The pad's loop is whole cycles, so the wrap is seamless; the iir
# voices are band-limited through the glide: no clicks, level held.
# scn: length 8b, seed 0, assets burst sine440
# expect: peak <= 0dbfs
# expect: peak >= -12dbfs
# expect: rms 0b..1b >= -30dbfs
# expect: rms 3b..4b >= -30dbfs
# expect: rms 6b..7b >= -30dbfs
# expect: no clicks
# expect: equals golden
voice drums from "burst" loop=forward gain=0.15
voice pad from "sine440" loop=forward pan=-1 gain=0.4
voice padc from "sine440" loop=forward pan=1 gain=0.4 resample=cubic
start drums pad padc
drums rate=3 over 6
pad rate=3 over 6
padc rate=3 over 6
